[DEBUG: Received AssistantMessage]
Now I understand! The "current sak" is determined by:
1. The sak subscription gets all saks where `finishedAt: null` (not finished)
2. The first (earliest) non-finished sak is the "current" sak

So to make a sak "current", I just need to:
1. Create a sak (it will have `finishedAt: null` by default)
2. It becomes automatically current since it's the only non-finished sak

So I don't need a `setSakCurrentDirect` function at all - just creating the sak is enough!

